{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793347599,"nonce":"liDHWtpGh0Xfaula8KSkh5dfzds=","title":"Bind browser recovery graphs to verified document identities","message":"Parent: 9d6a14bfc40bc5c2eb5a105609e1c2a1c37f3766d131dae8f4da586edd8b7b3c\n\nUse native stable document IDs for browser IndexedDB graphs and fence returning replicas before sending edits or saving. Migrate verified workspace/account-scoped path caches without deleting their graphs; retain late legacy updates and offline drafts. A closed moved document must recover its original graph at its new path; a file recreated at the old path must receive independent recovery. Pause live projections when their expected identity no longer owns the path. Keep hosted public identity/move capabilities disabled until coordinated cloud restoration and retargeting are available.\n\nValidate file and directory moves, path reuse, stale/offline reconnect, legacy migration and account isolation in real browser tests. Rebuild WASM and the session service, refresh both local services and prewarm the landing demo before closing this milestone. Live editor moves, personal history retargeting and cross-host ID import remain on the parent.","files":null}]}